From 16a4f3be5768ee6f5746ffb0b24d5cf3f6bdb47e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:33:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(world): finish flecs' OS API setup once, before the first
 world

flecs keeps its OS API (malloc, free, abort, the clock) in one
process-global C struct, and the first world fills it in without a lock.
flecs_ecs's ensure_initialized writes it after its claim mutex is
released, while ecs_mini copies the struct and writes it back. Two test
threads building their first worlds at once could therefore copy a
half-written struct. Then ecs_mini aborted on the ECS_MISSING_OS_API
check (SIGABRT, flecs.c:21288, captured under lldb) or called a NULL
hook (SIGSEGV).

new_world now runs ensure_initialized behind a std::sync::Once before it
builds any world, so the struct is complete and marked initialised
before any concurrent construction reads it.

Stress results, scripting suite, 8 copies x --test-threads=32: 7 crashes
in 1200 runs before the fix, 0 in 1600 after. The new world_init_race
binary re-runs itself as children that release 32 threads at a barrier
on loaded cores: 6 crashed children in 1920 before, 0 in 3840 after.

Fixes #379

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
